Open Season is a 2006 American animated adventure comedy film directed by Jill Culton
and Roger Allers and written by Nat Mauldin, Steve Bencich, and Ron J.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
Produced by Sony Pictures Animation, it features the voices of Martin
Lawrence, Ashton Kutcher, Gary Sinise, and Debra Messing.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
The film follows Boog, a domesticated grizzly bear, who is let go into the woods, and teams up with a
one-antlered mule deer named Elliot to return to his old home before open season starts.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
Open Season premiered at the Greek Theatre on September 25, 2006, and was released in
theaters in the United States on September 29 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed
$201 million against an $85 million budget.

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
The first in the Open Season film series, it was followed by Open Season 2
(2008), Open Season 3 (2010), and Open Season: Scared Silly (2015).

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
A video game based on the film was released, and a television series,
Open Season: Call of Nature, was released in 2023.

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of hunter, chase, bunny, garage, mountain.

20
